# Generated from: specs/22-give-maintainers-an-efficient-stewardship-workspace/requirements.md
Feature: Give maintainers an efficient stewardship workspace
  As a rotating volunteer maintainer
  I want prioritized work queues, reusable volunteer selection, understandable history, and safe handoff
  So that the schedule remains operable without specialist knowledge

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: Prioritized work leads to one narrow intervention
    Given <work> exists for a live or future commitment
    When a coordinator opens Home and prioritized Work
    Then both surfaces report the same authoritative count
    And each Work row has textual urgency and one direct intervention
    And rows are ordered by 24-hour urgent, 72-hour soon, then upcoming rules

    Examples:
      | work                         |
      | pending decision             |
      | uncovered commitment         |
      | unconfirmed volunteer        |
      | message not sent or bounced  |
      | recurring withdrawal risk    |
      | recurrence or handoff review |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Known volunteer search reveals only matching assignment data
    Given assignable, unrelated, and anonymized volunteer records exist
    When a coordinator posts the beginning of a name or email with at least three characters
    Then at most ten matching active names and full emails appear in stable order
    And phone, history, unrelated records, total count, and anonymized records do not appear
    When the coordinator selects a result that becomes stale
    Then assignment changes nothing and Search again is shown with preserved input

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Human history stays stable while new events arrive
    Given more than 50 matching audit events exist
    When a coordinator filters by local date, actor, shift, volunteer, and action category
    Then the newest 50 human local summaries appear without raw JSON, GUIDs, action codes, or tokens
    When a new event is inserted and the coordinator follows Next
    Then keyset paging neither duplicates nor skips the original matching sequence
    And tampered or mismatched cursor returns safely to newest matches

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Removed volunteer history remains non-identifying
    Given audit events correlate to an anonymized volunteer
    When a coordinator views matching history
    Then events use Removed volunteer and an opaque short reference
    And no original name, email, phone, raw identifier, or audit JSON appears

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Two coordinators verify handoff before removal
    Given OIDC is configured and two distinct normalized emails are allowlisted
    When each coordinator signs in independently and selects Verify my access
    Then Access shows both current-list verification dates and Handoff ready
    When the outgoing email is removed from external configuration
    Then its historical audit remains
    And it no longer counts toward readiness
    And no secret or shared credential is displayed or managed in-app

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Coordinator query work stays bounded as data grows
    Given representative PostgreSQL data has 1,000 volunteers, 5,000 shifts, and 10,000 audits
    When Home, Work, Requests, Coverage, Messages, History, and Search render full pages
    And the rendered-result volume is increased tenfold
    Then each surface remains within its fixed SQL-command budget
    And no per-row query, lazy loading, unbounded include, full-table load, or cache masking occurs

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Rotating coordinator completes daily stewardship without documentation
    Given a coordinator has no product training
    When they follow only application-visible Home and Work text
    Then they can resolve requests, coverage, delivery, withdrawal, and recurrence-review work
    And each task preserves valid input, offers one primary action, and ends with a plain-language next step
    And the workflow remains keyboard-usable at 320 CSS pixels
